"use strict";
// Published, reproducible checks; independent of the visitor's current selection.
function renderPredictionValidation(data) {
  const f=n=>n===null?'—':(Math.round((Number(n)+Number.EPSILON)*1000)/1000).toFixed(3)+'s';
  const rows=data.summary.map(r=>`<tr><td>+${r.h} lap${r.h===1?'':'s'}</td><td>${r.n} / ${r.eligible}</td><td>${f(r.modelMAE)}</td><td>${f(r.baselineMAE)}</td><td>${f(r.modelBias)}</td></tr>`).join('');
  const sessions=data.sessions.map(s=>`<tr><td>${esc(s.name)} · ${s.drivers.join(' / ')}</td>${s.horizons.map(h=>`<td>${h.n} / ${h.eligible}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('');
  const replacements=data.replacements.map(r=>`<tr><td>${r.session} · #${r.driver} · ${esc(r.compound)}</td><td>L${r.cutoffLap}</td><td>${r.ageZeroSupported?'Supported':'Withheld'}</td><td>${r.sourceFit?`${r.sourceFit.n} laps · ages ${r.sourceFit.minAge}–${r.sourceFit.maxAge}`:'No pre-stop same-compound fit'}</td></tr>`).join('');
  $('prediction-validation').innerHTML=`<h3>Recent-lap averaging was more accurate in this check</h3><p>The regression had higher mean absolute error at all three forecast horizons. This is a fixed retrospective check of the four bundled race datasets, with no tuning. Scored forecasts come from Austin and Monza; Las Vegas and Marina Bay have no supported forecasts on the eligible targets.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="analysis-table"><caption>Same-stint lap time · error in seconds</caption><thead><tr><th>Forecast</th><th>Scored / eligible targets</th><th>Regression MAE</th><th>Recent 3-lap mean MAE</th><th>Regression bias</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows}</tbody></table></div><p class="engineering-note">Positive bias means a slower predicted lap. MAE is average absolute error, not a confidence interval. Overlapping forecasts are not independent experiments; these errors are not bounds on strategy differences.</p><details class="race-section"><summary>Coverage and exclusions</summary><div><p>Each completed driver lap is an origin. Targets must stay in the same stint, avoid pit/neutralised laps and have ≥80% known front-interval coverage with ≤20% close-traffic exposure. Model gates then determine whether a forecast is available. The baseline uses the last three fit-eligible raw laps at the same cutoff.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="analysis-table"><thead><tr><th>Recorded race / drivers</th><th>+1 scored / eligible</th><th>+2</th><th>+3</th></tr></thead><tbody>${sessions}</tbody></table></div><p>Missing traffic coverage is not clean air. Unsupported ages and negative-trend extrapolation remain withheld. Detailed exclusion and hold counts are in the report data.</p></div></details><h3>Tyre replacement: fresh-set pace remains unvalidated</h3><p>Three observed changes reused a previously seen compound. All three withheld the age-zero estimate under the existing rules. The first five numbered laps of each new stint were checked; pit/outlaps and affected laps were excluded.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="analysis-table"><thead><tr><th>Session / driver / compound</th><th>Pre-stop cutoff</th><th>Age zero</th><th>Prior fit</th></tr></thead><tbody>${replacements}</tbody></table></div><p>In the Austin HAM example, ages 1–2 were supported even though age zero was not. Those two predictions were 0.841s and 0.927s slower than the observed laps. This limited transfer check does not validate warm-up, net pit loss or a complete stop scenario.</p><p><b>Use:</b> inspect conditional scenarios and their assumptions. The present regression has not demonstrated an accuracy advantage over the simple baseline, and replacement pace is not calibrated as a race outcome.</p><p><a href="./validation-report.md">Read the protocol and failure interpretation</a> · <a href="./data/prediction-validation.json" download>Download results</a></p>`;
}
function renderCaseFollowup(data) {
  const signed=n=>(n>0?'+':'')+Number(n).toFixed(3)+'s';
  const q2=data.q2Pairs[0],a22=data.traces.find(r=>r.lap===22).drivers;
  $('case-followup').innerHTML=`<h3>Follow-up: the minimum-speed difference does not explain S1 on its own</h3><p>Reprojecting both L22 traces onto the L25 reference gives sampled minima of ${a22[0].minimumSpeed}/${a22[1].minimumSpeed}km/h. Throttle recovery brackets still overlap, yet Norris is 0.086s slower in S1. The minimum-speed difference shrinks from 5km/h on L25 to 1km/h on L22. Tyre ages differ, so this is a counterexample to a simple explanation, not a controlled comparison.</p><p>The matching rule found only the original L25 pair in the bundled Q3 laps: same compound, start age and fresh-set flag, green status, starts within 60s, and neither lap more than 8% slower than its driver's phase best.</p>${q2?`<p>The same rule in Q2 selected L${q2.lapA}/L${q2.lapB}, with ages ${q2.age}/${q2.age} and starts ${q2.startSeparation.toFixed(3)}s apart. NOR−PIA sector differences were ${q2.sectorDelta.map(signed).join(' / ')}. S1 again favours Norris, but S3 is the largest difference. Native traces for this pair are not bundled, so the minimum-speed mechanism cannot be checked there.</p>`:''}<p><b>Conclusion:</b> retain the L25 observation; do not attribute the S1 gain to minimum speed alone or recommend a setup change. A second matched Q3 pair with native traces is still needed. <a href="./data/case-followup.json" download>Follow-up calculations</a>.</p>`;
}
async function loadPublishedCheck(file,id,render) {
  try {const response=await fetch('./data/'+file);if(!response.ok)throw Error();render(await response.json());}
  catch(_){$(id).innerHTML='<p>Historical check could not be loaded. <a href="./validation-report.md">Read the saved report</a>.</p>';}
}
loadPublishedCheck('prediction-validation.json','prediction-validation',renderPredictionValidation);
loadPublishedCheck('case-followup.json','case-followup',renderCaseFollowup);

$("open-prediction-validation").addEventListener("click",()=>{setAnalysisTab("model");$("panel-model").scrollIntoView({behavior:"smooth"});});

async function loadFullSessionAudit(){
  try{
    const [pace,race]=await Promise.all(['session-audit.json','race-availability.json'].map(async file=>{const r=await fetch('./data/'+file);if(!r.ok)throw Error();return r.json();}));
    const sessions=pace.sessions.filter(s=>!s.error),races=race.sessions.filter(s=>!s.error),count=a=>a.toLocaleString('en-US');
    const types=['Practice','Qualifying','Race'],label=t=>t==='Race'?'Race / Sprint':t==='Qualifying'?'Qualifying / Sprint qualifying':'Practice / testing';
    const pooled=(type,h,k)=>{const a=pace.groups.filter(g=>g.type===type).map(g=>g.horizons[h-1][k]),n=a.reduce((s,v)=>s+v.n,0);return {n,mae:n?a.reduce((s,v)=>s+v.n*(v.mae||0),0)/n:null};};
    const f=v=>v==null?'—':v.toFixed(3)+'s';
    $('full-session-audit').innerHTML=`<h3>${sessions.length} sessions checked · 2023–2026</h3><p>${sessions.filter(s=>s.available>0).length} sessions contain at least one three-lap pace estimate; ${sessions.filter(s=>s.trendAvailable>0).length} support the regression. Every recorded driver was inspected. ${pace.cancelled.length} cancelled entries are excluded. A one/two-lap reference is not counted as a forecast.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="analysis-table"><thead><tr><th>Session type</th><th>Sessions</th><th>Recent-3 estimate</th><th>Regression</th></tr></thead><tbody>${types.map(t=>{const a=sessions.filter(s=>s.type===t);return `<tr><td>${label(t)}</td><td>${a.length}</td><td>${a.filter(s=>s.available>0).length}</td><td>${a.filter(s=>s.trendAvailable>0).length}</td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>Availability means at least one supported driver and decision point, not every selection. Short qualifying runs usually provide only a measured reference.</p><h3>Existing race strategy: ${races.filter(s=>s.available>0).length} of ${races.length} sessions</h3><p>A supported default scenario exists at ${count(races.reduce((s,r)=>s+r.available,0))} of ${count(races.reduce((s,r)=>s+r.cutoffs,0))} inspected race cutoffs. This checks actual gaps and the existing tyre-age rules with H=12 and d=3; it does not validate which strategy would win.</p><details class="race-section"><summary>Forecast errors and scoring scope</summary><p>Traffic-unfiltered observed laps, same stint, no future slow-lap removal. Preparation/cooldown and changing run plans make practice and qualifying errors substantially larger. Compare methods only in the paired columns.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="analysis-table"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Horizon</th><th>Recent-3 count / MAE</th><th>Paired count</th><th>Recent-3 MAE · paired</th><th>Regression MAE · paired</th></tr></thead><tbody>${types.flatMap(t=>[1,2,3].map(h=>{const a=pooled(t,h,'recent'),b=pooled(t,h,'pairedRecent'),c=pooled(t,h,'trend');return `<tr><td>${label(t)}</td><td>+${h}</td><td>${count(a.n)} / ${f(a.mae)}</td><td>${count(c.n)}</td><td>${f(b.mae)}</td><td>${f(c.mae)}</td></tr>`;})).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>Overlapping forecasts are not independent experiments. All-session error populations differ from the initial traffic-filtered four-race check. These retrospective errors are not confidence intervals or bounds on strategy differences.</p></details><p><a href="./session-audit.md">Protocol, failures and reproduction</a> · <a href="./data/session-audit.json" download>All session results</a> · <a href="./data/race-availability.json" download>Race availability</a></p>`;
  }catch(_){$('full-session-audit').innerHTML='<p>The audit could not load. <a href="./session-audit.md">Read the saved all-session report</a>.</p>';}
}
loadFullSessionAudit();
